        "PMC8470387::web::011::3_3_high_temperature_friction_and_wear_p"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately 0.5 at.% W will induce stable lubricious oxide phases in CoCrFeNi.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The W-modified alloy will maintain lower friction and wear than CoCrFeNi from room temperature through 800 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8470387::web::011::3_3_high_temperature_friction_and_wear_p"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Baseline CoCrFeNi exhibits elevated friction and wear above approximately 500 °C.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxide-film breakdown and substrate softening cause the elevated high-temperature friction and wear of baseline CoCrFeNi.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed performance applies under moderate normal loads of approximately 5–10 N.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed performance applies in both air and inert atmospheres.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sliding produces a W-enriched oxide tribofilm that regulates friction and wear over the full temperature range.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "W promotes stable oxide islands within the tribofilm.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed oxide islands preserve low shear strength and prevent extensive abrasive or adhesive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to undoped CoCrFeNi, 0.5 at.% W will reduce friction by approximately 15–25% throughout 25–800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8470387::web::011::3_3_high_temperature_friction_and_wear_p"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to undoped CoCrFeNi, 0.5 at.% W will reduce wear volume by up to one order of magnitude throughout 25–800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8470387::web::011::3_3_high_temperature_friction_and_wear_p"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unmodified CoCrFeNi has friction coefficients exceeding approximately 0.4 under higher temperatures and normal loads.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "In AlCoCrFeNiWx coatings, 0.5 at.% W produced the minimum friction coefficient and wear loss after treatment at 800 °C for 60 minutes.",
      "field": "supporting_evidence",
